From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:32:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a5xx: render GMEM bins in raster order

On an a540 (chip_id 0x5040001) GTK4's GL renderer draws symbolic icons and
glyphs as solid quads in some frames when libcamera's GPU software ISP
submits from another context in the same process. The damage is confined
to bins of the rows fd_gmem's 'S' pattern renders right to left.

Measured on the device, frames with a solid-quad header icon (GPU ISP on,
GSK_RENDERER=gl), mesa 26.2.2 with this series' other a5xx patches:

  default                                   23/42, 18/22, 6/21
  FD_MESA_DEBUG=nobin                        0/19
  FD_MESA_DEBUG=sysmem                       0/19
  FD_MESA_DEBUG=nosbin (raster order)        0/22
  raster order for a5xx only                 0/11, 0/22, 0/22
  full restore before the first bin          9/22
  one-bin-wide VSC pipes, 'S' order kept    14/22
  CPU ISP / GSK cairo                        0/34, 0/12

Keeping the 'S' order but making every pipe one bin wide, so bins inside a
pipe are always visited in increasing n, does not help, and neither does
restoring all state before the first bin; the register state around the
binning pass is re-emitted by every submit. Only the traversal direction
matters. The blob programs CP_SET_BIN_DATA5 with the same raster index
within the pipe.

Skip the row swap on a5xx.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
index 2ee9b0b..fac9755 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -412,8 +412,14 @@ gmem_stateobj_init(struct fd_screen *screen, struct gmem_key *key)
    /* Swap the order of alternating rows to form an 'S' pattern, to improve
     * cache access patterns (ie. adjacent bins are likely to access adjacent
     * portions of textures)
+    *
+    * Not on a5xx: with hw binning, bins rendered right to left corrupt
+    * textured draws on an a540 (symbolic icons and glyphs come out as solid
+    * quads) when another context in the same process submits between
+    * frames. It does not depend on the order of bins inside a VSC pipe or on
+    * state left over for the first bin; only the direction does.
     */
-   if (!FD_DBG(NOSBIN)) {
+   if (!FD_DBG(NOSBIN) && !is_a5xx(screen)) {
       for (i = 0; i < gmem->nbins_y; i+=2) {
          unsigned col0 = gmem->nbins_x * i;
          for (j = 0; j < gmem->nbins_x/2; j++) {
-- 
